# ARMv8 Crypto Extensions for AES (added 2026-08-09).
#
# The Cortex-A53 cores advertise aes/pmull/sha2 in cpuinfo, but no kernel
# driver used them: every AES request fell back to aes-generic, so a dm-crypt
# volume measured 37 MB/s against 275-400 MB/s for the bare SSD. The CE
# implementations below make xts(aes) run on the hardware instructions
# (AES_ARM64_CE_BLK carries dm-crypt; NEON_BLK is the fallback path, GHASH_CE
# additionally provides gcm-aes-ce).
#
# The original audit plan also listed CRYPTO_SHA1/SHA2_ARM64_CE: those symbols
# no longer exist in 6.18 - SHA moved to lib/crypto and the accelerated lib
# versions are already built (CRYPTO_LIB_SHA256_ARCH=y). Only the crypto-API
# wrappers (CRYPTO_SHA256/512) are added so the algorithms are reachable
# through the API and AF_ALG.
#
# CRYPTO_USER_API_{HASH,SKCIPHER} expose algorithms over AF_ALG, which is what
# `cryptsetup benchmark` uses (it previously failed with "algif_skcipher not
# available"), so the speedup can actually be measured on the box.
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_CE_BLK=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES_ARM64_NEON_BLK=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_GHASH_ARM64_CE=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA256=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA512=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_HASH=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_USER_API_SKCIPHER=y
